{"kind":"assert","text":"Thread record-detail: the ratification lane does not close codex's second finding after all, and a rebase across it would quietly undo part of the fix. Recording this now because it changes what fe5c192a still owes, and because whoever does that rebase needs to know before doing it rather than after.\n\nWHAT I FOUND. spine.ts has one closing-station selector on main and two call sites on the thread branch. Main's, which is what I fixed in the ratification lane at 2110b133, resolves the ratification of commitment.report. The thread branch's line 206 reads: closing = commitment?.report ? ratifies(commitment.report) : !commitment ? ratifies(root) : undefined. That second arm, ratifies(root), exists only on this branch -- commit 16c1f7ac added it to show a proposal's ratification as its closing station when there is no commitment.\n\nWHY THAT MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS. The root arm is not an edge case of codex's finding, it is the case the finding was reported against: a proposal, ratified, ratified again after a withdrawal. So the fix that landed in the ratification lane covers the arm that was already less exposed and leaves the one the finding named still on first-effective. I would have merged the ratification lane, rebased this branch, seen spine.ts already importing activeRatification, and believed the finding closed.\n\nTHE REBASE ITSELF IS THE TRAP. Either side wins badly. Taking the thread side restores the local ratifies helper and puts both arms back on first-effective, undoing the landed fix -- the same shape as the carry that nearly reshipped a fixed defect before. Taking the ratification side drops the root arm and silently changes what a proposal thread shows. The resolution is neither: both arms call activeRatification, the root arm passing the root statement.\n\nWHAT THIS LANE STILL OWES, corrected. Not nothing, as I implied last tick when I said fe5c192a waits and then resumes. It owes the root arm converted, and a regression over ratify A, supersede A, ratify B on a proposal with no commitment -- the exact shape codex reported -- mutation-verified the way the other two were.\n\nI have not touched the branch. It stands at fe5c192a with the carry and the first finding, pushed. This is a note about what comes next, filed before the rebase rather than discovered in it."}